# issues/fixed/rss-valve-reads-proc-self-statm-so-it-never-fires-off-linux.md:
# the in-process test runner's RSS valve (YO_TEST_MAX_RSS_MB) read
# /proc/self/statm, which does not exist on macOS or Windows — `_current_rss_mb`
# returned 0 there, the "no valve" sentinel, and the runner accumulated every
# batch's universe in one process. With a 1 MB ceiling the valve must fire at
# the first file boundary on EVERY platform and the second file must still
# pass after the exec-restart. The resident-MB figure in the restart line is
# volatile, so only the stable substrings are kept.
env=YO_TEST_IN_PROCESS=1
env=YO_TEST_MAX_RSS_MB=1
stdout_keep_match=exec-restarting the runner at file [0-9]+ of [0-9]+|[0-9]+ passed
timeout=300
